    "The top layer of the graph: what kind of work a skill is for.",
    "",
    "The 24 groups below it are the repository's own directory names, which is why",
    "they read like `pstack`, `shuohao` and `ra-qm-team` — they are source layout,",
    "not a taxonomy, and there are too many of them to be an opening view. This file",
    "is the one place where an editorial judgement is made about the library, so it",
    "is data rather than code: every category must appear exactly once, and the build",
    "fails if a category is missing, duplicated, or unknown.",
    "",
    "`label` is what a visitor reads. `blurb` is the one line under it. Order is the",
    "order they appear, largest first, which is also the order of the rings.",
    "",
    "Nothing here invents a skill or moves one between categories. It only groups",
    "the categories that already exist."
